    {
      "index": 134,
      "start": 357.55,
      "end": 357.56,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So here I switched directly to writing"
    },
    {
      "index": 135,
      "start": 357.56,
      "end": 361.71,
      "duration": 4.15,
      "text": "down"
    },
    {
      "index": 136,
      "start": 364.91,
      "end": 364.92,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "in cosine and sine in the in the"
    },
    {
      "index": 137,
      "start": 364.92,
      "end": 367.63,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "forms, but we could also have kept it in"
    },
    {
      "index": 138,
      "start": 367.64,
      "end": 368.63,
      "duration": 0.99,
      "text": "the"
    },
    {
      "index": 139,
      "start": 368.64,
      "end": 370.63,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "complex form if we were solving the"
    },
    {
      "index": 140,
      "start": 370.64,
      "end": 372.71,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "equation in complex space. And then we"
    },
    {
      "index": 141,
      "start": 372.72,
      "end": 374.27,
      "duration": 1.55,
      "text": "would just have complex exponentials"
    },
    {
      "index": 142,
      "start": 374.28,
      "end": 376.71,
      "duration": 2.43,
      "text": "here with the frequencies omega angular"
    },
    {
      "index": 143,
      "start": 376.72,
      "end": 377.99,
      "duration": 1.27,
      "text": "frequency one."
    },
    {
      "index": 144,
      "start": 378.0,
      "end": 380.27,
      "duration": 2.27,
      "text": "So this is the homogeneous equation the"
    },
    {
      "index": 145,
      "start": 380.28,
      "end": 382.19,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "homogeneous"
    },
    {
      "index": 146,
      "start": 382.2,
      "end": 384.67,
      "duration": 2.47,
      "text": "solution for this"
    },
    {
      "index": 147,
      "start": 384.68,
      "end": 386.19,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "homogeneous constant coefficient"
    },
    {
      "index": 148,
      "start": 386.2,
      "end": 388.15,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "differential equations. But what do we"
    },
    {
      "index": 149,
      "start": 388.16,
      "end": 390.51,
      "duration": 2.35,
      "text": "see? We can see that it's exactly the"
    },
    {
      "index": 150,
      "start": 390.52,
      "end": 392.63,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "same form that the solution that we had"
    },
    {
      "index": 151,
      "start": 392.64,
      "end": 394.55,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "previously, right?"
    },
    {
      "index": 152,
      "start": 394.56,
      "end": 396.95,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "And so the question here is this"
    },
    {
      "index": 153,
      "start": 396.96,
      "end": 400.71,
      "duration": 3.75,
      "text": "oscillator overdamped or underdamped?"
    },
    {
      "index": 154,
      "start": 400.72,
      "end": 402.43,
      "duration": 1.71,
      "text": "And as we see here we're going to have"
    },
    {
      "index": 155,
      "start": 402.44,
      "end": 404.75,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "oscillations that are damped by a co-"
    },
    {
      "index": 156,
      "start": 404.76,
      "end": 406.75,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "factor by a pre-factor of decaying"
    },
    {
      "index": 157,
      "start": 406.76,
      "end": 409.71,
      "duration": 2.95,
      "text": "exponential minus 3t for both cases."
    },
    {
      "index": 158,
      "start": 409.72,
      "end": 412.31,
      "duration": 2.59,
      "text": "So this is decaying, so there is"
    },
    {
      "index": 159,
      "start": 412.32,
      "end": 414.07,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "differently damping and we can see that"
    },
    {
      "index": 160,
      "start": 414.08,
      "end": 416.15,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "here because we had a positive value for"
    },
    {
      "index": 161,
      "start": 416.16,
      "end": 418.31,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "B which is the damping term in the in"
    },
    {
      "index": 162,
      "start": 418.32,
      "end": 420.15,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "the oscillator system."
    },
    {
      "index": 163,
      "start": 420.16,
      "end": 421.909,
      "duration": 1.749,
      "text": "But there is there are still"
    },
    {
      "index": 164,
      "start": 421.919,
      "end": 423.909,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "oscillations because we had a"
    },
    {
      "index": 165,
      "start": 423.919,
      "end": 425.51,
      "duration": 1.591,
      "text": "discriminant that was negative which"
    },
    {
      "index": 166,
      "start": 425.52,
      "end": 427.75,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "introduced complex numbers hence cosines"
    },
    {
      "index": 167,
      "start": 427.76,
      "end": 430.75,
      "duration": 2.99,
      "text": "and sines. So basically oscillations."
    },
    {
      "index": 168,
      "start": 430.76,
      "end": 432.15,
      "duration": 1.39,
      "text": "Therefore we're in the case of an"
    },
    {
      "index": 169,
      "start": 432.16,
      "end": 433.67,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "underdamped"
    },
    {
      "index": 170,
      "start": 433.68,
      "end": 435.11,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "response"
    },
    {
      "index": 171,
      "start": 435.12,
      "end": 447.07,
      "duration": 11.95,
      "text": "uh an underdamped system."
    },
    {
      "index": 172,
      "start": 448.59,
      "end": 448.6,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Discriminant"
    },
    {
      "index": 173,
      "start": 448.6,
      "end": 450.59,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "was negative."
    },
    {
      "index": 174,
      "start": 450.6,
      "end": 459.87,
      "duration": 9.27,
      "text": "So for the last part"
    },
    {
      "index": 175,
      "start": 462.23,
      "end": 462.24,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "of this problem, we now leave this"
    },
    {
      "index": 176,
      "start": 462.24,
      "end": 464.15,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "differential equation, which was second"
    },
    {
      "index": 177,
      "start": 464.16,
      "end": 466.51,
      "duration": 2.35,
      "text": "order, and move to higher order"
    },
    {
      "index": 178,
      "start": 466.52,
      "end": 468.43,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "differential equations of eighth order."
    },
    {
      "index": 179,
      "start": 468.44,
      "end": 470.91,
      "duration": 2.47,
      "text": "And we're given"
    },
    {
      "index": 180,
      "start": 470.92,
      "end": 474.35,
      "duration": 3.43,
      "text": "eight roots."
    },
    {
      "index": 181,
      "start": 475.95,
      "end": 475.96,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "4"
    },
    {
      "index": 182,
      "start": 475.96,
      "end": 480.71,
      "duration": 4.75,
      "text": "plus or minus 5i"
    },
    {
      "index": 183,
      "start": 482.99,
      "end": 483.0,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "We have the root three, which is real,"
    },
    {
      "index": 184,
      "start": 483.0,
      "end": 485.11,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "which is repeated three times."
    },
    {
      "index": 185,
      "start": 485.12,
      "end": 487.87,
      "duration": 2.75,
      "text": "And the root 4 plus or minus 5i, which"
    },
    {
      "index": 186,
      "start": 487.88,
      "end": 490.27,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "is repeated two times. So, we saw before"
    },
    {
      "index": 187,
      "start": 490.28,
      "end": 492.35,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "then when we have repeated roots, that"
    },
    {
      "index": 188,
      "start": 492.36,
      "end": 494.31,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "means that we would have, let's say, in"
    },
    {
      "index": 189,
      "start": 494.32,
      "end": 495.99,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "a a second order differential equation,"
    },
    {
      "index": 190,
      "start": 496.0,
      "end": 497.07,
      "duration": 1.07,
      "text": "we'd have"
    },
    {
      "index": 191,
      "start": 497.08,
      "end": 498.67,
      "duration": 1.59,
      "text": "in this case a discriminant that would"
    },
    {
      "index": 192,
      "start": 498.68,
      "end": 500.31,
      "duration": 1.63,
      "text": "be equal to zero, and we would need to"
    },
    {
      "index": 193,
      "start": 500.32,
      "end": 501.909,
      "duration": 1.589,
      "text": "introduce an a different type of"
    },
    {
      "index": 194,
      "start": 501.919,
      "end": 503.19,
      "duration": 1.271,
      "text": "solutions, because instead of"
    },
    {
      "index": 195,
      "start": 503.2,
      "end": 506.59,
      "duration": 3.39,
      "text": "introducing exponential of plus"
    },
    {
      "index": 196,
      "start": 506.6,
      "end": 509.11,
      "duration": 2.51,
      "text": "RT exponential minus RT, now we don't"
    },
    {
      "index": 197,
      "start": 509.12,
      "end": 510.95,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "have the minus RT, so we need to seek"
    },
    {
      "index": 198,
      "start": 510.96,
      "end": 512.63,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "another type solution, and we multiply"
    },
    {
      "index": 199,
      "start": 512.64,
      "end": 514.43,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "the exponential by T."
    },
    {
      "index": 200,
      "start": 514.44,
      "end": 516.55,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "So, one type of solution for this unique"
    },
    {
      "index": 201,
      "start": 516.56,
      "end": 519.43,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "root that would come out would be just"
    },
    {
      "index": 202,
      "start": 519.44,
      "end": 522.27,
      "duration": 2.83,
      "text": "2T. For the first"
    },
    {
      "index": 203,
      "start": 522.28,
      "end": 525.23,
      "duration": 2.95,
      "text": "of the triple root, it would be a 3T."
    },
    {
      "index": 204,
      "start": 525.24,
      "end": 527.47,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "For the second one, we would have"
    },
    {
      "index": 205,
      "start": 527.48,
      "end": 530.95,
      "duration": 3.47,
      "text": "a T 3T. For the third one, we need to go"
    },
    {
      "index": 206,
      "start": 530.96,
      "end": 534.95,
      "duration": 3.99,
      "text": "higher order."
    },
    {
      "index": 207,
      "start": 537.75,
      "end": 537.76,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "3T. Now, we have complex roots, so that"
    },
    {
      "index": 208,
      "start": 537.76,
      "end": 539.67,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "gives us solutions of the same form that"
    },
    {
      "index": 209,
      "start": 539.68,
      "end": 542.63,
      "duration": 2.95,
      "text": "we found in questions A and B."
    },
    {
      "index": 210,
      "start": 542.64,
      "end": 543.55,
      "duration": 0.91,
      "text": "So, I'm going to just going to just"
    },
    {
      "index": 211,
      "start": 543.56,
      "end": 545.03,
      "duration": 1.47,
      "text": "write them"
    },
    {
      "index": 212,
      "start": 545.04,
      "end": 546.91,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "here."
    },
    {
      "index": 213,
      "start": 546.92,
      "end": 550.07,
      "duration": 3.15,
      "text": "Where now we have E"
    },
    {
      "index": 214,
      "start": 550.08,
      "end": 552.03,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "4T"
    },
    {
      "index": 215,
      "start": 552.04,
      "end": 555.63,
      "duration": 3.59,
      "text": "cosine 5T"
    },
    {
      "index": 216,
      "start": 555.64,
      "end": 559.27,
      "duration": 3.63,
      "text": "plus E 4T"
    },
    {
      "index": 217,
      "start": 561.829,
      "end": 561.839,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "sine 5T."
    },
    {
      "index": 218,
      "start": 561.839,
      "end": 563.55,
      "duration": 1.711,
      "text": "And for the repeated root, it's the same"
    },
    {
      "index": 219,
      "start": 563.56,
      "end": 565.19,
      "duration": 1.63,
      "text": "game, even though we're in complex"
    },
    {
      "index": 220,
      "start": 565.2,
      "end": 566.87,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "roots, it's the same idea. We need to"
    },
    {
      "index": 221,
      "start": 566.88,
      "end": 581.51,
      "duration": 14.63,
      "text": "multiply all of it by T."
    },
    {
      "index": 222,
      "start": 583.59,
      "end": 583.6,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So these are the families of linearly"
    },
    {
      "index": 223,
      "start": 583.6,
      "end": 586.03,
      "duration": 2.43,
      "text": "independent roots that would come out"
    },
    {
      "index": 224,
      "start": 586.04,
      "end": 588.27,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "and linearly independent solutions that"
    },
    {
      "index": 225,
      "start": 588.28,
      "end": 590.23,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "would come out of these roots. So now"
    },
    {
      "index": 226,
      "start": 590.24,
      "end": 592.55,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "the general solution is simply the"
    },
    {
      "index": 227,
      "start": 592.56,
      "end": 594.55,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "linear combination of all these linearly"
    },
    {
      "index": 228,
      "start": 594.56,
      "end": 597.95,
      "duration": 3.39,
      "text": "independent functions."
    },
    {
      "index": 229,
      "start": 597.96,
      "end": 599.43,
      "duration": 1.47,
      "text": "So we will now introduce different"
    },
    {
      "index": 230,
      "start": 599.44,
      "end": 605.63,
      "duration": 6.19,
      "text": "constants."
    },
    {
      "index": 231,
      "start": 607.15,
      "end": 607.16,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "C5"
    },
    {
      "index": 232,
      "start": 607.16,
      "end": 609.31,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "C6"
    },
    {
      "index": 233,
      "start": 609.32,
      "end": 610.99,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "C7"
    },
    {
      "index": 234,
      "start": 611.0,
      "end": 612.43,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "and C8."
    },
    {
      "index": 235,
      "start": 612.44,
      "end": 615.11,
      "duration": 2.67,
      "text": "And we have eight indeterminate"
    },
    {
      "index": 236,
      "start": 615.12,
      "end": 617.67,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "text": "coefficients to to to deal with because"
    },
    {
      "index": 237,
      "start": 617.68,
      "end": 620.47,
      "duration": 2.79,
      "text": "these would be eight roots of an eighth"
    },
    {
      "index": 238,
      "start": 620.48,
      "end": 622.39,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "order polynomial. And so if we were to"
    },
    {
      "index": 239,
      "start": 622.4,
      "end": 623.79,
      "duration": 1.39,
      "text": "solve an initial value problem like"
    },
    {
      "index": 240,
      "start": 623.8,
      "end": 625.79,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "that, we would need eight different"
    },
    {
      "index": 241,
      "start": 625.8,
      "end": 627.71,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "types of initial conditions to determine"
    },
    {
      "index": 242,
      "start": 627.72,
      "end": 629.95,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "the values of these constants."
    },
    {
      "index": 243,
      "start": 629.96,
      "end": 631.91,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "So to summarize, we use the"
    },
    {
      "index": 244,
      "start": 631.92,
      "end": 633.99,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "characteristic polynomial method to"
    },
    {
      "index": 245,
      "start": 634.0,
      "end": 636.55,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "text": "solve these these problems and"
    },
    {
      "index": 246,
      "start": 636.56,
      "end": 638.35,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "introducing"
    },
    {
      "index": 247,
      "start": 638.36,
      "end": 639.99,
      "duration": 1.63,
      "text": "higher order equations than the first"
    },
    {
      "index": 248,
      "start": 640.0,
      "end": 640.99,
      "duration": 0.99,
      "text": "order"
    },
    {
      "index": 249,
      "start": 641.0,
      "end": 642.87,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "differential equations we saw before."
    },
    {
      "index": 250,
      "start": 642.88,
      "end": 646.11,
      "duration": 3.23,
      "text": "And what is important to remember is the"
    },
    {
      "index": 251,
      "start": 646.12,
      "end": 648.27,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "the different type of solutions that you"
    },
    {
      "index": 252,
      "start": 648.28,
      "end": 651.11,
      "duration": 2.83,
      "text": "get depending on the roots of the"
    },
    {
      "index": 253,
      "start": 651.12,
      "end": 652.99,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "characteristic polynomial and the sign"
    },
    {
      "index": 254,
      "start": 653.0,
      "end": 654.39,
      "duration": 1.39,
      "text": "of the discriminant. So whether the"
    },
    {
      "index": 255,
      "start": 654.4,
      "end": 657.39,
      "duration": 2.99,
      "text": "roots are real or purely imaginary or"
    },
    {
      "index": 256,
      "start": 657.4,
      "end": 659.59,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "imaginary number will give three types"
    },
    {
      "index": 257,
      "start": 659.6,
      "end": 662.03,
      "duration": 2.43,
      "text": "of the behavior. The critically damped"
    },
    {
      "index": 258,
      "start": 662.04,
      "end": 663.87,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "behavior, if it's real then it's going"
    },
    {
      "index": 259,
      "start": 663.88,
      "end": 666.55,
      "duration": 2.67,
      "text": "to be just overdamped behavior, and if"
    },
    {
      "index": 260,
      "start": 666.56,
      "end": 668.55,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "the roots are complex then it will be an"
    },
    {
      "index": 261,
      "start": 668.56,
      "end": 670.63,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "underdamped behavior. Now when we are"
    },
    {
      "index": 262,
      "start": 670.64,
      "end": 672.95,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "given different type of roots with"
    },
    {
      "index": 263,
      "start": 672.96,
      "end": 674.47,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "repeated roots, it's important to know"
    },
    {
      "index": 264,
      "start": 674.48,
      "end": 676.59,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "how to construct the solutions as well."
    },
    {
      "index": 265,
      "start": 676.6,
      "end": 678.59,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "And that's by introducing new types of"
    },
    {
      "index": 266,
      "start": 678.6,
      "end": 679.99,
      "duration": 1.39,
      "text": "function where we're multiplying by"
    },
    {
      "index": 267,
      "start": 680.0,
      "end": 681.95,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "polynomial in"
    },
    {
